    "content": "National Siblings Day is celebrated annually on April 10th to honor the special, lifelong bond between brothers and sisters. Founded by Claudia Evart in 1995 to honor her late siblings, this day promotes appreciating siblings, reconnecting, and celebrating, often by sharing memories, photos, or spending time together.Key Aspects and Traditions of Siblings Day:Purpose: The day focuses on recognizing the重要 (important) role siblings play in our lives, similar to Mother’s or Father’s Day.How to Celebrate: Common activities include calling or visiting siblings, sharing childhood photos on social media, treating them to a meal, or sending a thoughtful message.Origins: Claudia Evart selected April 10th in memory of her late sister, Lisette.Recognition: While not a federal holiday, governors in 49 states have issued proclamations to recognize the day.Popular social media hashtags for the day include #NationalSiblingsDay and #SiblingLove. View all National Siblings Day is celebrated annually on April 10th to honor the special, lifelong bond between brothers and sisters. Founded by Claudia Evart in 1995 to honor her late siblings, this day promotes appreciating siblings, reconnecting, and celebrating, often by sharing memories, photos, or spending time together. Key Aspects and Traditions of Siblings Day: Purpose: The day focuses on recognizing the重要 (important) role siblings play in our lives, similar to Mother’s or Father’s Day. How to Celebrate: Common activities include calling or visiting siblings, sharing childhood photos on social media, treating them to a meal, or sending a thoughtful message. Origins: Claudia Evart selected April 10th in memory of her late sister, Lisette. Recognition: While not a federal holiday, governors in 49 states have issued proclamations to recognize the day. Popular social media hashtags for the day include #NationalSiblingsDay and #SiblingLove.",
